Fixed. The issue was in `JsonPrimitive.equals` (gson/src/main/java/com/google/gson/JsonPrimitive.java:311), which compared integral values via `Number#longValue()`, truncating large `BigInteger`s to their low 64 bits.

The fix compares integral primitives as `BigInteger` instead:

```java
if (isIntegral(this) && isIntegral(other)) {
  return getAsBigInteger().equals(other.getAsBigInteger());
}
```

This preserves cross-type equality (e.g. `Integer 10` equals `BigInteger("10")`, and `hashCode` stays consistent since small `BigInteger` hashes match the long-based hash), while distinct large `BigInteger`s now compare unequal. Full gson module suite passes: 1248 tests, 0 failures (including the new `testEqualsIntegerAndBigInteger` case).
